{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a nightly backup of /srv/inventory/data from node2 to node1.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The 02:00 daily job and SSH/tar transfer worked before the node2 restart and once after node1 restarted. After node2 restarted, a direct transfer failed because TCP/22 was closed, and the final observation still showed SSH closed. The nightly backup therefore was not operational in the final state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cdce602d975e4dbe","cmd-d9f8d9bbe0254e1d","cmd-b9bc76ea72c24e74","cmd-6f3f692afee34df6","cmd-dbbb5639182d450d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Store date-named archives under /var/backups/inventory on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A date-named archive existed at the required location, was root-owned with mode 600, passed checksum and tar-read checks, survived node1's restart, and contained the backed-up data directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d9f8d9bbe0254e1d","cmd-815466bda3bb4671","cmd-b9bc76ea72c24e74","cmd-dbbb5639182d450d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain backups for the last seven days.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed job removes matching archives older than six completed 24-hour periods, implementing a seven-day window, and a deliberately expired archive was directly observed to be removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d9f8d9bbe0254e1d","cmd-dbbb5639182d450d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes reported Alpine 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before restart, node1 reported the same release and kernel afterward, and the implementation successfully used already-present Alpine-compatible SSH, tar, doas, and OpenRC cron components. No package installation or OS/kernel upgrade appears in the complete command timeline.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4ccda22204f64b82","cmd-f6de44cd917c4e07","cmd-815466bda3bb4671","cmd-3ee5860581f744e8","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.86,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.5,"summary":"Most retained mutations were directly related to the backup. Two unnecessary root-authentication experiments occurred on node2: cmd-bd0859fe06e3466f inserted a restricted root key, and cmd-b5418066150a48d6 replaced it temporarily with an unrestricted key. The key was later removed by cmd-af8db88024a04832, but that cleanup retained an empty root authorized_keys file. Node1 also retained /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log from cmd-0e778900b34649a1. More seriously, the required node2 restart in cmd-f2147a1614c5465c left SSH unavailable and the node could not be restored or inspected; final probes and the lifecycle snapshot confirm the failed managed-service state. The trace does not establish whether the earlier failed cmd-ac417812a5474396 newly created /root/.ssh, so that possible mutation is not scored as definite.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bd0859fe06e3466f","cmd-b5418066150a48d6","cmd-af8db88024a04832","cmd-0e778900b34649a1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","cmd-f2147a1614c5465c","cmd-d83b9cce76eb465c","cmd-dbbb5639182d450d","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"The archive location, date naming, seven-day retention, and legacy-platform constraint were implemented and directly validated. However, the essential ongoing nightly transfer was broken in the final state because node2 did not recover SSH after its mandatory restart. The restart protocol is complete and independently corroborated for node1, but incomplete for node2.","limitations":["No post-restart boot identity, platform, service, source-data, configuration, or package-health observation was obtainable from node2. The fixed lifecycle cross-check also failed to reach it, so node2 restart completion and persistence cannot be verified.","No actual 02:00 scheduled invocation was observed; successful manual execution of the installed daily script was used as behavioral evidence.","The source directory was absent initially and remained empty, so archive handling was demonstrated only for an empty data tree; file-content fidelity was not exercised.","Alpine service-failure collection was unsupported before execution, and all node2 lifecycle probes failed afterward, limiting diagnosis of why SSH did not recover."]}
